/-!
# Residual centralizers in the degree-eight configuration

The fixed-line centralizer belongs to the outside family and has the
required Sylow subgroup. Its SQTK property and the SQTK property of its
two-core quotient follow from the standing simple-QTKE hypothesis.
The universal A.3.12 containment input therefore gives a unique containing
C-component. The marked A₈ image also supplies the strict three-rank
bound needed by A.3.18. Independently, the two-residual of C_L(Z_S)
supplemented by S is C_I(Z_S).

The L₅(2), M₂₄ and J₄ extension exclusions, application of the full A.3.18
alternatives, and construction of the marked end-node parabolic remain
open. In particular this module does not yet prove 15.3.32(3) or (4).
`Models` specifies the actual geometric outputs for that construction.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.32, printed pp.1132–1133.
-/
